ps5: close idle curl sessions off the application thread.

CApplication::ProcessSlow() calls DllLibCurlGlobal::CheckIdle() on the app
(GUI) thread every ~500 ms. CheckIdle() tore down each session idle for >30 s
(multi_remove_handle / easy_cleanup / multi_cleanup) while holding
m_critSection. Tearing down a keep-alive HTTPS connection to a slow mirror can
block in TLS/socket shutdown until curl's timeout (tens of seconds); on the PS5
this froze the GUI for ~35 s while browsing the add-on repository (a mirror
connection went idle after a skin download, then its close blocked), and held
the global curl lock so every other transfer stalled too.

CheckIdle() now only splices the expired, non-busy sessions out of the live
pool under the lock (fast) and defers their teardown to a background CJob, so
the potentially-blocking curl cleanup never runs on the app thread and never
holds the lock. Each closed session was already idle and not busy, so no other
thread references its handles. If the job manager cannot accept the job (e.g.
during shutdown) the teardown is done inline so handles are not leaked.

